@startuml layers
title individuals-api - target layer structure

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "api (generated)" <<Frame>> {
  interface AuthApi
  note right of AuthApi
    Generated from individuals-api.yaml
    with interfaceOnly. The controller
    implements it, so the contract and
    the code cannot drift apart.
  end note
}

package rest {
  class AuthController
}

package service {
  class RegistrationService
  class AuthenticationService
}

package gateway {
  class PersonServiceGateway <<@Component>>
  class KeycloakAdminGateway <<@Component>>
  class KeycloakOidcGateway <<@Component>>
}

package validation {
  class PasswordsMatchValidator
}

package error {
  class GlobalExceptionHandler
  class SecurityErrorWriter
}

package logging {
  class RequestLogFilter
  class RequestLog
}

package config {
  class SecurityConfig
  class HttpClientsConfig
}

package util {
  class KeycloakClaims
}

package metrics {
  class AuthMetrics
}

AuthController ..|> AuthApi
AuthController --> RegistrationService
AuthController --> AuthenticationService

RegistrationService --> PersonServiceGateway
RegistrationService --> KeycloakAdminGateway
RegistrationService --> KeycloakOidcGateway
AuthenticationService --> KeycloakOidcGateway

RegistrationService --> AuthMetrics
AuthenticationService --> AuthMetrics
AuthenticationService --> KeycloakAdminGateway
AuthenticationService --> KeycloakClaims

note bottom of gateway
  individuals-api owns no data, so it has no
  repository. The gateway takes that seat: one
  class per external system, injected through
  the constructor. No interface in front of it -
  a second implementation would be the reason to
  add one, and there is none.

  Nothing above this layer may see person-client
  types or Keycloak's own shapes. Only the domain
  user_uid and our own types cross upwards.
end note

note bottom of logging
  Not a layer of its own - it wraps every request.
  RequestLogFilter runs before the security chain,
  and RequestLog carries the fields across thread
  hops so every record of a request is complete.
end note

note bottom of error
  Controllers declare throws Exception, so
  errors land here and become one ErrorResponse
  carrying the traceId. SecurityErrorWriter is
  the second road: what the filter chain rejects
  never reaches an advice.
end note

@enduml
